# Citation File Format 1.2.0 -- https://citation-file-format.github.io/
# Keep "version" equal to photonix.__version__ (tests/test_metadata.py checks it)
# and set "date-released" when the release is tagged (see RELEASING.md).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use photonix in published work, please cite it using the metadata
  below, together with the specific version (and, once available, the Zenodo
  DOI of that version) you used.
type: software
title: "photonix: accuracy-first, differentiable photonic integrated circuit design"
abstract: >-
  photonix is an accuracy-first Python toolkit for photonic integrated circuit
  design. It connects differentiable compact models, S-parameter circuit
  simulation, finite-difference eigenmode, EME and FDFD electromagnetic
  solvers, layout and GDSII exchange, process-variation and yield analysis, and
  external verification hand-offs through one port and data model, on a JAX
  backend with a NumPy fallback.
authors:
  - name: "photonix contributors"
version: 0.2.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/mayank-lang/photonix"
url: "https://github.com/mayank-lang/photonix"
keywords:
  - photonics
  - silicon photonics
  - photonic integrated circuits
  - S-parameters
  - circuit simulation
  - mode solver
  - inverse design
  - differentiable programming
  - JAX
